  "body": "Each of your {Ally} assets gains the {Yithian} trait.\n⭕ After you commit a card to a skill test you are performing: Double the skill icons on that card. (Limit once per test.)\n⭐ effect: +2. Draw 1 card.",
  "flavor": "Curiosity was my crime. Humanity, my sentence.",
  "illustrator": "Stephen Somers",
  "card_number": "16",
  "encounter_group_number": "",
  "picture_base64": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
  "image_mode": 1,
  "back": {
    "name": "🏅Yithian",
    "subtitle": "A Curious Explorer",
    "class": "中立",
    "card_back": {
      "other": "【Additional Requirements】: Your deck must include cards with at least 4 unique {Traits}, with a minimum of 5 cards for each of those {Traits} (<i>20 cards total</i>).\n【Additional Options】: * Increase the level limit for cards by (X – 4) (to a maximum of 3), where X is the number of unique traits that are included on at least 5 of your cards in your deck",
      "story": "For countless cycles, he observed the churning path of human thought and emotion with fascination deemed grotesque by his kind. Among the ageless minds of the Great Race of Yith, such curiosity was considered perilous—self-corrupting. Exiled from the crystal halls of Pnakotus, he was cast adrift in alien epochs, until he took root in a new host: a linguist among a Miskatonic expedition in the dark heart of the Amazon. Now, he walks the streets of Arkham in a borrowed form, documenting everything, mimicking laughter, rehearsing empathy, annotating fear. Though he passes as human, his affect is uncanny, his gaze unblinking, and his questions... uncomfortable. Yet he alone senses the ripples of something ancient stirring beneath the veil of human ignorance. Something even his kind chose to forget.",
      "size": 30,
      "option": "Cards level 0-2* from any class.",
      "requirement": "Thirst for Knowledge, Forgotten Knowledge, 1 random basic weakness."
    },
